// Regression case for the build_pattern divergence (NOT fixed by fc46e9db):
// an empty `\u{}` escape inside a `like` pattern must be a parse error. Cedar
// rejects `like "\u{}"` with `the input \u{} is not a valid escape`.
//
// The current build_pattern parses the braced body with
// `u32::from_str_radix("", 16)`, which fails, then falls into its "malformed --
// pass through" branch and emits `\`, `u`, `{`, `}` as literal pattern chars --
// accepted and validated cleanly instead of rejected.
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when { context.input.document like "\u{}" };
